<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lon Nol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lon Nol was a Cambodian general and politician who served as defence minister and prime minister under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a>. On 18 March 1970, while Sihanouk was abroad, he and the national assembly deposed him, and Lon Nol proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Republic, becoming its president in 1972. Backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, his government fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> and North Vietnamese until he fled in April 1975. He died in the United States.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lon-nol.jpg" alt="Lon Nol" width="320" height="503" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LonNol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>On 18 March 1970 Cambodia's national assembly, led by Prime Minister <b>Lon Nol</b> and Prince Sisowath Sirik Matak, voted to remove Norodom Sihanouk as head of state while he was abroad.</blockquote><a href="/state/khmer-republic">Khmer Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>On 18 March 1970, while Sihanouk was abroad, the national assembly deposed him, and <b>Lon Nol</b> proclaimed the Khmer Republic.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970)</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Pou Rieng District, in what is now <a href="/countries/cambodia">Cambodia</a>. Died in Fullerton, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=11.55,105.26&amp;year=1959" aria-label="Pou Rieng District on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7446 1733 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Lon Nol"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7896 2003h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7896 2003h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=11.55,105.26&amp;year=1959">What was here in 1959? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
